From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:29:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3568: RG DS: a slot on trial boots with the
 watchdog running

A slot on trial that hangs before systemd takes the hardware watchdog
over (in the kernel, mounting the root, or in userspace before PID 1)
never restarted: only a panic used up its try. SPL now starts the
RK3568's dw_wdt when it boots a slot on trial; Linux's dw_wdt finds it
running and keeps it fed until systemd opens it, within the command
line's watchdog.open_timeout. A good slot boots with the watchdog off,
as before, and holding A is still checked first.

The watchdog runs in IRQ mode, two stages of 11.2 s: the first stage's
interrupt panics the kernel (dw_wdt keeps the mode, kernel
generic/0006; the panic pre-timeout governor) and the panic restarts
the board through the RK817 PMIC. The watchdog's own reset, the second
stage, is a CRU global reset, which this board never comes back from
(it hangs before SPL): found on the device, a slot on trial whose
init never started stayed dark until switched off by hand.

Upstream status: board-specific, not for upstream (nibOS's own scheme).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c
index 75d4902b..6ea72acf 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3568/rk3568.c
@@ -278,6 +278,7 @@ bool rockchip_dwmmc_board_no_uhs(void)
 #include <memalign.h>
 #include <mmc.h>
 #include <u-boot/crc.h>
+#include <asm/io.h>
 #include <asm/unaligned.h>
 
 /*
@@ -293,6 +294,7 @@ bool rockchip_dwmmc_board_no_uhs(void)
  * same rules.
  */
 #define AB_SLOT_B		0x10000		/* sectors: 32 MiB */
+#define AB_WDT			0xfe600000	/* the RK3568's dw_wdt */
 #define AB_BLOCK		(0x20000 - 2)	/* the partition's last KiB */
 
 static bool ab_valid(const u8 *s)
@@ -301,6 +303,28 @@ static bool ab_valid(const u8 *s)
 	       crc32(0, s, 508) == get_unaligned_le32(s + 508);
 }
 
+/*
+ * A slot on trial boots with the watchdog running, so a hang anywhere before
+ * systemd takes the watchdog over (the kernel, the root, userspace before
+ * PID 1 opens it) restarts the device and uses up the try, as a panic does.
+ * IRQ mode, two stages of TOP 12 (2^28 cycles of the 24 MHz tclk, 11.2 s).
+ * Linux's dw_wdt finds it running, keeps the mode and feeds it
+ * (WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED) for as long as watchdog.open_timeout on the
+ * command line allows, until systemd opens it. If nothing does, the first
+ * stage's interrupt panics the kernel (the panic pre-timeout governor) and
+ * the panic restarts the board through the RK817 PMIC. The second stage, a
+ * CRU global reset, is left for a kernel that can't take the interrupt:
+ * this board doesn't come back from that one (it hangs before SPL).
+ * A good slot boots with it off, as before.
+ */
+static void ab_watchdog(void)
+{
+	writel(12 << 4 | 12, AB_WDT + 0x04);	/* TORR: TOP_INIT, TOP */
+	writel(0x76, AB_WDT + 0x0c);		/* CRR: restart the count */
+	/* CR: reset pulse 256 pclk, IRQ mode (RMOD), on */
+	writel(7 << 2 | BIT(1) | 1, AB_WDT + 0x00);
+}
+
 static unsigned long ab_pick(struct mmc *mmc, unsigned long base)
 {
 	ALLOC_CACHE_ALIGN_BUFFER(u8, buf, 2 * 512);
@@ -333,6 +357,7 @@ static unsigned long ab_pick(struct mmc *mmc, unsigned long base)
 	if (blk[6 + a]) {
 		blk[6 + a]--;
 		printf("A/B: slot %c on trial, %d tries left\n", 'A' + a, blk[6 + a]);
+		ab_watchdog();
 	} else if (blk[8 + o]) {
 		blk[5] = o;
 		printf("A/B: slot %c failed, back to slot %c\n", 'A' + a, 'A' + o);
-- 
2.56.0

